      "parts": [{
        "text": "In real life, raw IR sensors (like the TCRT5000 or"
      }, {
        "text": " QTR sensors used in line followers) are **Analog**. They output a voltage between 0V and 5V depending on"
      }, {
        "text": " how much infrared light is reflected back (white reflects a lot, black absorbs it). \n\nMany cheap Arduino starter kits attach a comparator chip ("
      }, {
        "text": "like the LM393) to the sensor to convert that analog wave into a simple Digital `HIGH/LOW` based"
      }, {
        "text": " on a little blue potentiometer. \n\nHowever, since you want **raw data** for advanced robotics (like PID line"
      }, {
        "text": " following), we need to activate the **ADC (Analog-to-Digital Converter)** peripheral inside our virtual ATmega328p CPU"
      }, {
        "text": "!\n\nI have upgraded the physics engine so that the IR sensor is now \"smart\":\n*   If you connect the"
      }, {
        "text": " IR sensor to an **Analog Pin (A0 - A5)**, the simulation calculates the exact pixel darkness and feeds a simulated 0"
      }, {
        "text": "V - 5V signal into the virtual ADC. You can read it using `analogRead()`, which will return"
      }, {
        "text": " `0` (Pure White) to `1023` (Pure Black).\n*   If you connect it to a **Digital"
      }, {
        "text": " Pin (D2 - D13)**, it acts like a cheap LM393 module, thresholding the"
      }, {
        "text": " color at 50% gray and outputting a strict `HIGH` or `LOW` for `digitalRead()`.\n\n"
      }, {
        "text": "### Code Updates\n\nReplace your `App.jsx` with the updated code below. Notice that I added `AVR"
      }, {
        "text": "ADC` to the imports, changed the default pin to `A0`, and updated the default Arduino code to print the raw analog"
      }, {
        "text": " numbers to the Serial Monitor.\n\n```jsx\nimport React, { useState, useRef, useEffect } from \u0027react\u0027;"
      }, {
        "text": "\nimport Editor from \u0027@monaco-editor/react\u0027;\nimport { Play, Square, RotateCcw, Monitor"
      }, {
        "text": ", Settings, Terminal, Crosshair, GripVertical, GripHorizontal, Download, Upload, RefreshCcw, FileUp"
      }, {
        "text": ", ImagePlus, Trash2, Wrench, PlusCircle, X, Box } from \u0027lucide-react\u0027;"
      }, {
        "text": "\nimport Matter from \u0027matter-js\u0027;\nimport { \n  CPU, avrInstruction, \n  "
      }, {
        "text": "AVRTimer, timer0Config, timer1Config, timer2Config, \n  AVRUSART, us"
      }, {
        "text": "art0Config,\n  AVRADC, adcConfig // \u003c-- Added the Virtual ADC Peripheral\n} from \u0027avr8js\u0027; "
      }, {
        "text": "\n\nfunction loadHex(source, target) {\n  for (const line of source.split(\u0027\\n\u0027)) {"
      }, {
        "text": "\n    if (line[0] \u003d\u003d\u003d \u0027:\u0027 \u0026\u0026 line.substring(7, 9) \u003d\u003d\u003d \u002700"
      }, {
        "text": "\u0027) {\n      const bytes \u003d parseInt(line.substring(1, 3), 16);\n      "
      }, {
        "text": "const addr \u003d parseInt(line.substring(3, 7), 16);\n      for (let i"
      }, {
        "text": " \u003d 0; i \u003c bytes; i++) {\n        target[addr + i] \u003d parseInt(line."
      }, {
        "text": "substring(9 + i * 2, 11 + i * 2), 16);\n      "
      }, {
        "text": "}\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nconst getPinState \u003d (cpu, pin) \u003d\u003e {\n  "
      }, {
        "text": "let portAddr, bit;\n  if (pin \u003e\u003d 0 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 7) { portAddr \u003d"
      }, {
        "text": " 0x2B; bit \u003d pin; } \n  else if (pin \u003e\u003d 8 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d"
      }, {
        "text": " 13) { portAddr \u003d 0x25; bit \u003d pin - 8; } \n"
      }, {
        "text": "  else if (pin \u003e\u003d 14 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 19) { portAddr \u003d 0x2"
      }, {
        "text": "8; bit \u003d pin - 14; } \n  else { return false; }\n  return ("
      }, {
        "text": "cpu.data[portAddr] \u0026 (1 \u003c\u003c bit)) !\u003d\u003d 0;\n};\n\n// Directly write HIGH"
      }, {
        "text": " or LOW to the PIN registers (simulating external physical digital signals)\nconst setExternalPin \u003d (cpu, pin"
      }, {
        "text": ", isHigh) \u003d\u003e {\n  let pinAddr, bit;\n  if (pin \u003e\u003d 0 \u0026\u0026 pin"
      }, {
        "text": " \u003c\u003d 7) { pinAddr \u003d 0x29; bit \u003d pin; }  // PIND\n"
      }, {
        "text": "  else if (pin \u003e\u003d 8 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 13) { pinAddr \u003d 0x23"
      }, {
        "text": "; bit \u003d pin - 8; } // PINB\n  else if (pin \u003e\u003d 14 \u0026\u0026 pin"
      }, {
        "text": " \u003c\u003d 19) { pinAddr \u003d 0x26; bit \u003d pin - 14; }"
      }, {
        "text": " // PINC\n  else { return; }\n\n  if (isHigh) {\n    cpu.data["
      }, {
        "text": "pinAddr] |\u003d (1 \u003c\u003c bit);\n  } else {\n    cpu.data[pinAddr] \u0026\u003d"
      }, {
        "text": " ~(1 \u003c\u003c bit);\n  }\n};\n\nconst generateId \u003d () \u003d\u003e Math.random().toString(3"
      }, {
        "text": "6).substr(2, 9);\n\nconst TYPE_TAGS \u003d {\n  dc_motor: \u0027"
      }, {
        "text": "DC MOTOR\u0027,\n  imu: \u0027IMU\u0027,\n  ir_sensor: \u0027IR SENSOR\u0027,\n  "
