        "text": " 90.0;\n    if (targetHeading \u003e\u003d 360) targetHeading -\u003d 36"
      }, {
        "text": "0; // Keep it bounded 0-360\n    \n    Serial.print(\"New Target: \");\n    Serial.println"
      }, {
        "text": "(targetHeading);\n  } \n  else if (error \u003e 0) {\n    // We need to turn Right\n    digitalWrite"
      }, {
        "text": "(MOTOR_LEFT, HIGH);\n    digitalWrite(MOTOR_RIGHT, LOW);\n  }"
      }, {
        "text": " \n  else {\n    // We need to turn Left\n    digitalWrite(MOTOR_LEFT, LOW);\n    digital"
      }, {
        "text": "Write(MOTOR_RIGHT, HIGH);\n  }\n  \n  delay(20); // Small delay for stability\n}\n```\n\n###"
      }, {
        "text": " What to watch for:\n* Watch the **Serial Monitor**: You will see the heading updating rapidly. The moment it gets within"
      }, {
        "text": " 5 degrees of the target, the motors snap off.\n* Watch the **SYS_TELEMETRY Angle**:"
      }, {
        "text": " You can verify that the raw physics engine angle matches the math output in your serial monitor!\n* Try **manually dragging** the robot"
